        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pete Dexter, Elie Wiesel, Daniel Baldwin, Lee Tamahori, Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, John Malkovich\n- Works: Mulholland Falls, Vampires, The Pandora Project, Stealing Candy, Paparazzi, Grey Gardens\n- Roles: novelist, writer, professor, political activist, Nobel Laureate, Holocaust survivor, director, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Elie Wiesel was born on September 30, 1928, and he was a Romanian-born American Jewish writer, professor, political activist, Nobel Laureate, and Holocaust survivor.\n- Pete Dexter was born on July 22, 1943, and he is an American novelist.\n- Mulholland Falls is a 1996 American neo-noir crime thriller film directed by Lee Tamahori and written by Pete Dexter.\n- Mulholland Falls stars Nick Nolte, Jennifer Connelly, Chazz Palminteri, Michael Madsen, Chris Penn, Melanie Griffith, Andrew McCarthy, Treat Williams, and John Malkovich.\n- Daniel Baldwin had starring roles in Mulholland Falls in 1996, Vampires in 1998, The Pandora Project in 1998, Stealing Candy in 2002, Paparazzi in 2004, and Grey Gardens in 2009.\n- Elie Wiesel died on July 2, 2016.",
